        "original_id": "296c21ee-d706-593e-a175-0956dd1c065d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Johnny Majors, Paul Hornung, Antone Davis\n- Organizations: Tennessee Volunteers football, Green Bay Packers, National Football League, Southeastern Conference\n- Places: Neyland Stadium, Knoxville, Tennessee\n- Awards: Heisman Trophy, All-American honors, Pro Football Hall of Fame\n- Events: 1956 Heisman Trophy voting, 1990 Tennessee Volunteers football season, Super Bowl\n\nFacts:\n- In 1956, Johnny Majors finished second to Paul Hornung in voting for the Heisman Trophy.\n- Paul Hornung was born on December 23, 1935.\n- From 1957 to 1966, Paul Hornung played professional football for the Green Bay Packers of the National Football League.\n- Paul Hornung won four NFL titles and the first Super Bowl with the Green Bay Packers.\n- In 1990, Johnny Majors was the head coach of the Tennessee Volunteers football team in his 14th year.\n- In 1990, the Tennessee Volunteers football team played as a member of the Southeastern Conference and played its home games at Neyland Stadium in Knoxville, Tennessee.\n- Before his junior year at Tennessee, Antone Davis was moved to right offensive tackle.\n- In 1990, Antone Davis earned unanimous All-American honors as a senior for Tennessee.",
